@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] share-moment-shooting-star
After something is shared into ThyMind, while it saves, the share target MUST play
the shooting star moment over the app that shared: the page blurs under a night
sky, a constellation draws itself, one star breaks off and falls, turning colour
once for a Rare find and twice for a Legendary one, lands in a white-out, and the
find's card spins out of it face up with its rarity, stars and points. The card
then turns over into the tag step (share-tag-step-icon-grid); when that ends it
turns back and flies into the backpack at the top right, whose count goes up, as
the page comes back. A tap anywhere or Back while it plays MUST skip the rest of
it and the tag step: the page comes back at once and the find pops into the
backpack. When nothing could be saved the moment MUST fade without the backpack
and the share sheet says why (share-problems-speak-for-thymind). With the
system's animations turned off the share sheet shows instead. The moment MUST
NOT show levels or XP, and the backpack MUST NOT be called a basket.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026, 23:09: "Let's make the 03 shooting star one into a
real thing in the app and build it out fully", moment 03 of the Inventory share
moment prototype; the tap to skip, the backpack and no levels come from his
feedback on that prototype the same day.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] share-tag-step-icon-grid
The tag step after the shooting star MUST be an icon grid on the back of the
find's card, grown to fill the screen at the card's shape. It shows the spaces
as a row of chips, one chosen at a time, with the space ThyMind suggests already
chosen; a Search tags field that can add a new tag; and a grid of tiles, each a
line icon, the tag's name and a check: ThyMind's own tags first, on and marked
with the spark (share-sheet-shows-thymind-tags), then the user's, then recent
tags, off. A tap on a tile puts its tag on or takes it off. It MUST go by itself
as share-sheet-fades-by-itself says, its button showing the time left; a tap
outside the card or Back closes it at once. The spaces and tags chosen MUST reach
the saved cards however it closes.
Source: Tavi's pick of M9 Icon grid on 5 November 2026, 23:27, for the tag step
that follows the shooting star. Choosing the suggested space from the start is
the M9 frame of the Inventory canvas; the icon for each tag is Claude's choice.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] find-rarity-from-library
A find's rarity MUST come from the user's own library, never from chance or
payment: Legendary when no earlier card in the gallery comes from the same
source, Rare when fewer than 5 do, and Common otherwise. A link's source is its
site, without www., m. or mobile., with twitter.com read as x.com and youtu.be
and music.youtube.com as youtube.com; a file's or note's source is its kind.
Rarity sets the star's colours, the card's stars (1, 3, 5) and its points (10,
40, 80). When the library cannot be counted before the star breaks off, the find
is Common.
Source: Tavi's rules for Inventory, 5 November 2026: rarity comes from the
user's own library and points reward saving. The thresholds, the sources and
the point values are Claude's choice and not yet confirmed.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] share-moment-sounds
The moment's sounds MUST play only while the phone's ringer is on, never when it
is silent or on vibrate, and its vibrations MUST follow the phone's touch
feedback setting.
Source: the sound and feel of the Inventory share moment prototype Tavi heard on
5 November 2026; following the ringer and the touch feedback setting is Claude's
choice.
